        "original_id": "60783b5e-9f76-5d41-8cb4-d4878973eba0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kendrick Lamar, DJ Dahi, Drake, Jay Rock, Big Sean, Ariana Grande, Dacoury Natchel, Michael Carlson, Leland Wayne\n- Works: “Money Trees”, Good Kid, M.A.A.D City, Section.80, “Worst Behavior”, “Research” \n- Roles: rapper, recording artist, producer\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, Kendrick Lamar released his debut studio album Section.80 exclusively through the iTunes Store as an independent album.\n- In 2012, Kendrick Lamar released Good Kid, M.A.A.D City as his second studio album.\n- “Money Trees” is a song by American hip hop recording artist Kendrick Lamar from his major-label debut studio album Good Kid, M.A.A.D City.\n- “Money Trees” features Kendrick Lamar’s label-mate Jay Rock.\n- DJ Dahi is noted for producing Drake’s “Worst Behavior” and Kendrick Lamar’s critically acclaimed album track “Money Trees.”\n- The song “Research” was written by Big Sean, Ariana Grande, Dacoury Natchel, Michael Carlson, and Leland Wayne, and it was produced by DJ Dahi and Metro Boomin.",
